$Id: README.internals,v 1.1 2011/05/11 16:12:46 drmiller Exp $

Communication between the Front End and the simulator is via two pipes,
one for each direction. All communication is in units of uint16_t.

The simulator reads and interprets the following codes on it's input pipe:

(hex)
00kk	Keyboard code 'kk' was entered. E.g. the user presses "Search" and
	the code 0080 is sent to the simulator on the pipe.

010k	"Special" key: PRIME, SET P.C., VERIFY PROG, RECORD PROG, and SHIFT
	variations. 'k' is the ucode address to jump to:
	0 = PRIME
	1 = VERIFY PROG
	2 = SET P.C.
	3 = RECORD PROG
	4 = S.M.
	5 = B.S.
	6 = INS
	7 = DEL

02mm	Mode register 0 changed, new value is 'mm'.
	b0 = FP/Sc
	b1 = List or Learn-and-Print
	b2 = Learn or Learn-and-Print
	b3 = Step

03mm	Mode register 1 changed, new value is 'mm'.
	b0 = Rad/Deg
	b1 = Printer On
	b2 = n.c.
	b3 = n.c.

04bb	Tape read data, byte 'bb'.

[TBD: I/O for "CN-36"]


The simulator sends the following codes on it's output pipe:

00sc	Display refresh data. 's' is digit select, 'c' is digit code.
01sc	Note, traffic is "optimized" such that once a couple copies have
02sc	been sent, the simulator stops sending until a key is pressed.
03sc	Bits 8 and 9 indicate the current state of the Mach Err and
	Prog Err lights, respectively. Either one of those results in
	a flickering display.

04bb	Tape "record" data, byte 'bb'. Implies "Tape On"(?).

0500	Tape Off.

08cd	Printer data, 'c' is column (overflows into lo bit of '8'),
	'd' is drum code (character to print). 'c' value > 19 means
	(print and) feed. Note, column/drum values are not sent in
	a contiguous pattern. All columns for drum '0' (if any) are
	sent at once, then all columns for drum '1', etc. A 'feed'
	command that does not follow column/drum data prints a blank
	line.

10cc	Print data for "CN-24" (IBM Selectric?). 'cc' is a 6-bit
	"rotate/tilt" code for the output device.
	[TBD: what constitutes a CR-LF?]

[TBD: I/O for "CN-36"]
